use `discardOut` normalizer and test error cases (ExitCode: 1) since no TTY available in test env\n     - Tests: default-no-tty, all-flag, all-long, save-flag, save-long, file-dev-null, file-long, set-echo, set-neg-echo, help, version\n     ```go\n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gstty\")\n         if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n         discardOut := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n             {Name: \"default-no-tty\", ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardOut}},\n             // ... more tests\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/stty/display.go, cmd/stty/flags.go, cmd/stty/settings.go** — NOT YET READ\n     - These files contain critical existing implementation code referenced by main.go\n     - Must be read before implementing to understand existing patterns for `applySettings`, flag definitions, display logic\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reading was performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Initial file reading phase was completed for the SRD, main.go, and test file\n   - The key gap is that the other stty source files (display.go, flags.go, settings.go) have NOT been read yet, and they contain the implementation details needed to extend the code properly\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task description including role, repository context, project documentation (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, roadmap), execution constitution, coding standards, go style constitution, and detailed task requirements for implementing srd105-stty R5.1, R6.1, R6.2, R7.1\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\